# Database & API Patterns

## Supabase clients

- `src/config/supabase.ts` — single client, exported as `supabase`
- `src-max/config/supabase.ts` — two clients: `supabase` (Max DB) + `tgSupabase` (TG DB for battery_requests)

## Tables

| Table | Key columns |
|-------|-------------|
| `users` | `user_id`, `username` |
| `warranty_reminders` | `user_id`, `battery_name`, `start_date`, `duration`, `next_service_date`, `paused` |
| `broadcasts` | `id`, `text`, `date`, `time`, `sent` |
| `bot_messages` | `message_id`, `chat_id`, `broadcast_id` |
| `battery_requests` | `id`, `user_id`, `brand`, `model`, `engine`, `year`, `delivery`, `phone`, `status`, `source` |

## Battery requests source

Always set `source` field when creating a battery request:
- `'tg'` — from Telegram bot
- `'max'` — from Max bot (written to TG Supabase via `tgSupabase`)
- `'website'` — from website

## API calls

Product data comes from `GET ${API_URL}/api/products?id=`. Images served from `${API_URL}/storage/app/public/{image}`.

All axios calls go through `src/config/api.ts` (axios instance with `baseURL`).

## All DB calls in services/

Never call `supabase` directly from commands or lib. Always use a `Service` method:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const reminders = await WarrantyService.getReminders();

// ❌ BAD — DB query in command handler
const { data } = await supabase.from('warranty_reminders').select('*');
```
